      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$\\frac12\\times8^2\\times\\theta=\\frac{16\\pi}{3}$, so $\\theta=\\frac\\pi6$. B1 — SOI OE, e.g. $2\\pi/12$ or 0.524 (3 s.f.); degrees acceptable if used consistently. Arc length $=8\\times\\text{their }\\pi/6=4.1887\\ldots$. M1 — OE FT their $\\theta$; look for $4\\pi/3$. $BC=2\\times8\\sin(\\frac12\\times\\text{their }\\pi/6)=4.1411\\ldots$. M1 — FT their $\\theta$; look for $16\\sin(\\pi/12)$ or $4\\sqrt6-4\\sqrt2$. Alternative for this M1: cosine rule $BC^2=8^2+8^2-2(8)(8)\\cos(\\text{their }\\pi/6)$; or Pythagoras from lengths 4 and $4\\sqrt3$; or sine rule $BC/\\sin(\\pi/6)=8/\\sin(5\\pi/12)$. Perimeter $=8.33$. A1 AWRT; must be one combined term. Total 4.",
